# desk-parse's Courier mode (ADR 0097, amended by the draft ADR "Courier's store" section 4): the Courier sandbox runs
# java @/app/courier-parse.options once per message, deskd's connection as the worker's stdin and stdout, with an empty
# environment. The JVM flags are parse.options' own, line for line (courier-parse's OptionsTest compares them), so the two
# workers in the sandbox have the same heap, the same security manager and the same silence; then the Courier mode's two
# properties, the classpath (courier-parse and its jars are in /app/lib, as desk-agent's dependencies), the main class and
# --from-stream.
# - ma.courier.trackers: ADR 0076's tracker hosts, one a line, which the image's bake writes from the Browser blocker's
#   pinned EasyPrivacy list and the sandbox mounts read-only over the empty placeholder this image ships. Read once, before
#   the worker's security manager is installed.
-Xmx72m
-Xms8m
-Xss512k
-XX:+UseSerialGC
-XX:TieredStopAtLevel=1
-XX:MaxMetaspaceSize=96m
-XX:+ExitOnOutOfMemoryError
-XX:-HeapDumpOnOutOfMemoryError
-XX:-CreateCoredumpOnCrash
-XX:ErrorFile=/dev/null
-XX:-UsePerfData
-XX:+DisableAttachMechanism
-XX:+DisplayVMOutputToStderr
-Xlog:disable
-Xlog:all=warning:stderr
-Xshare:auto
-Djava.awt.headless=true
-Djava.security.manager=allow
-Dma.courier.debug=false
-Dma.courier.trackers=/app/courier/trackers.txt
-cp
/app/desk-agent.jar
com.minimalistalliance.desk.courier.parse.CourierWorker
--from-stream
